 a late shift in the national environment in the final weeks could move this toward either candidate.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 66 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Tom Barrett (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 7th is an even-partisan district where first-term Republican Tom Barrett faces Democrat William Lawrence in one of the nation's most expensive House races at over $51 million spent. The national environment favors Democrats this year, and most race raters call the seat a tossup leaning toward a flip, while prediction markets give Lawrence roughly a 60-65% chance of winning.\n\nBarrett holds traditional incumbent advantages, including a large cash-on-hand edge, and Speaker Mike Johnson has campaigned with him. Lawrence has drawn heavy Democratic surrogate support, including Bernie Sanders, and leads 49-47 in the most recent poll, though that survey is Democratic-sponsored and two months old. With sparse polling and heavy outside spending on both sides, the race sits in a narrow Democratic-favored band.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7073, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7167, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7145, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6654, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6515, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6531, "margin": 3.0}, {"d